          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_3a9aef510b28223ab4ba",
          "document_start": 130,
          "document_end": 268,
          "text": "These regions are separated by a diaphragm that can burst very quickly and contain one gas at high pressure and another at lower pressure.",
          "section_id": "section_c47a27f38420",
          "start": 130,
          "end": 268,
          "chunk_start": 130,
          "chunk_end": 268,
          "sentence_document_start": 130,
          "sentence_document_end": 268,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_8c553d9f85932e70b87b",
          "document_start": 269,
          "document_end": 361,
          "text": "The gases could be different (thus, all their properties as well) as can their temperatures.",
          "section_id": "section_c47a27f38420",
          "start": 269,
          "end": 361,
          "chunk_start": 269,
          "chunk_end": 361,
          "sentence_document_start": 269,
          "sentence_document_end": 361,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_3378748cf60ce5fbbd00",
          "document_start": 362,
          "document_end": 571,
          "text": "Below the graphic of the shock tube is a pressure vs. distance plot showing that the pressure in region 4 (the high-pressure region) is greater than that in region 1, and the diaphragm divides the two regions.",
          "section_id": "section_c47a27f38420",
          "start": 362,
          "end": 571,
          "chunk_start": 362,
          "chunk_end": 571,
          "sentence_document_start": 362,
          "sentence_document_end": 571,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_3d78b301fc5a3c901a82",
          "document_start": 572,
          "document_end": 799,
          "text": "If the diaphragm bursts, then a shock will propagate into the lower pressure region, increasing the pressure, and a rarefaction wave (to be discussed later) will propagate into the high-pressure region, decreasing the pressure.",
          "section_id": "section_c47a27f38420",
          "start": 572,
          "end": 799,
          "chunk_start": 572,
          "chunk_end": 799,
          "sentence_document_start": 572,
          "sentence_document_end": 799,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_24da9663f9779ee99295",
          "document_start": 800,
          "document_end": 962,
          "text": "If we examine the shock tube after some very short time  $t$ , the situation will appear as shown in Figure 2.29 with the corresponding pressure-distance profile.",
          "section_id": "section_c47a27f38420",
          "start": 800,
          "end": 962,
          "chunk_start": 800,
          "chunk_end": 962,
          "sentence_document_start": 800,
          "sentence_document_end": 962,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_6ab5c9a8456b4ea1b5f8",
          "document_start": 963,
          "document_end": 1223,
          "text": "One of the most interesting aspects of compressible fluid flow is that if we know what the initial states of the ideal gases in the shock tube are, we can predict the pressures and temperatures of the unsteady motion afterward by Equations 2.161 through 2.171.",
          "section_id": "section_c47a27f38420",
          "start": 963,
          "end": 1223,
          "chunk_start": 963,
          "chunk_end": 1223,
          "sentence_document_start": 963,
          "sentence_document_end": 1223,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sentence_871f9853f339721bf55d",
          "document_start": 1224,
          "document_end": 1290,
          "text": "In fact, we can predict the pressure behind the initial shock from",
          "section_id": "section_c47a27f38420",
          "start": 1224,
          "end": 1290,
          "chunk_start": 1224,
          "chunk_end": 1290,
          "sentence_document_start": 1224,
          "sentence_document_end": 1290,
          "sentence_complete": true
        },
